1
00:00:01,980 --> 00:00:04,290
[Episode 3]

2
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:05,620
Who is it?

3
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:09,000
Let me use the bathroom.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,490
Who is it?

5
00:00:10,490 --> 00:00:15,130
The bathroom... Let me use the bathroom!

6
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:17,250
This isn't the public restroom!

7
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:20,690
I'm going to pee my pants.

8
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:22,500
Let me use the bathroom.

9
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,910
Then go! I won't stop you.

10
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:26,770
What a psycho!

11
00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:53,700
Hey, you!

12
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:03,020
Hey! Australia, right?

13
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:07,720
Right? Right? Australia, in Melbourne.

14
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:16,360
Don't you remember me?

15
00:01:17,130 --> 00:01:18,270
No.

16
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:22,110
I'm pretty sure...

17
00:01:23,090 --> 00:01:24,760
Do you live here?

18
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:26,000
Yes.

19
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:29,630
Maybe he's not the same person?

20
00:01:29,630 --> 00:01:31,300
Is this your house?

21
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:33,660
No, it's not mine.

22
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:36,180
We just rent out the basement.

23
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:40,180
This house is a rich person's house, right?

24
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:43,980
Yes.

25
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,730
So...

26
00:01:50,830 --> 00:01:52,830
Is it a really rich family's house?

27
00:01:56,890 --> 00:02:01,930
But hey! Why would you pee on someone's house?

28
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:05,480
Why would you do that?

29
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:07,470
You peed here!

30
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:11,900
I marked this place as my territory. Why?

31
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,180
What?

32
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:16,940
Dogs mark their territory like this.

33
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:20,200
What the... Why would this be your territory?

34
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:24,040
See you again. I'll come to pee again tomorrow.

35
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,680
What's with him?

36
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:35,130
So is he saying that he's a dog? What?

37
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:40,150
That's right. I'm a dog.

38
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:44,700
Not a human being. A dog!

39
00:02:48,950 --> 00:02:52,680
Your mom was a famous movie star a long time ago...

40
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:55,500
And your brother is one of
the top singers in our country.

41
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,900
Nice, huh?

42
00:03:45,610 --> 00:03:49,790
We looked for the orphanage
you and your sister are from.

43
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:54,030
You two are twins.

44
00:04:08,210 --> 00:04:11,850
What a psycho!

45
00:04:11,850 --> 00:04:13,450
Eww! How disgusting.

46
00:04:16,070 --> 00:04:17,500
How filthy!

47
00:04:23,538 --> 00:04:25,997
A million dollars!

48
00:04:34,950 --> 00:04:36,001
Are you Korean?

49
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:39,420
You're Korean?

50
00:04:45,090 --> 00:04:50,600
I have a husband! And kids!

51
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:54,360
Just go to sleep. If you don't want to die.

52
00:04:56,930 --> 00:04:59,440
[Start paying attenshun crazee brat]

53
00:05:20,610 --> 00:05:23,120
Jason sent you here, didn't you?

54
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:26,350
Jason sent you here to kill me!

55
00:05:26,350 --> 00:05:27,940
Did you think I'll get tricked?

56
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:30,380
Do you really think I was going
to get tricked by you, old man!

57
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:32,380
How can that lady be my mom?

58
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:34,180
How can that lady be my mom?

59
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:36,520
She is your mother!

60
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:38,690
Don't lie!

61
00:05:38,690 --> 00:05:42,830
If she's so great, why would she abandon me?

62
00:05:42,830 --> 00:05:48,900
With that money, she can buy all the milk
in the world and raise 1,000 children!

63
00:05:50,230 --> 00:05:55,460
It's not like life was hard on her,
or that she's starving.

64
00:05:55,460 --> 00:06:02,480
How? Not one but two? How could she?

65
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:05,070
Your mom is that kind of lady.

66
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:13,950
Anything that gets in her way, she'll throw away!

67
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:23,040
She's capable of that. Your mom does what she wants.

68
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:27,240
Shut your mouth. I'm going to kill you.

69
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:29,350
I'm going to kill you, old man!

70
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:42,470
Grandpa, I want to die!

71
00:06:42,470 --> 00:06:48,120
Why, did your mom cause an accident again?

72
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:52,820
I don't want her as my mom! I want to die!

73
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:55,880
Why? What'd she do this time?

74
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:58,500
She's not my mom!

75
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:02,510
I can't live with her!

76
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:32,150
Did he come looking for me? All the way from Australia?

77
00:07:34,990 --> 00:07:37,230
But how'd he know where I live?

78
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:40,460
Is he a psycho?

79
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:46,800
Hey, Yun.

80
00:07:48,610 --> 00:07:50,310
Pork?

81
00:07:50,310 --> 00:07:53,620
I'm going to put it in the sauce for noodles.

82
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:57,090
It's not in your fridge? Would you buy some?

83
00:07:57,090 --> 00:07:59,090
The side meat.

84
00:07:59,090 --> 00:08:01,260
Okay. Thanks.

85
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:04,040
I'm an excellent cook.

86
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:08,480
Fried pork. Braised beef. Noodles. Pasta.

87
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:11,200
I also clean, wash dishes,
and do laundry extremely well.

88
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:14,920
There's nothing I can't do well, to be honest.

89
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:17,010
Later, I probably can raise babies well.

90
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:20,300
You won't have to lift a finger.

91
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:25,600
I guess we'll just have to wait and see.

92
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:29,080
But I think I'd make an excellent husband.

93
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:31,130
Do you like me that much?

94
00:08:31,130 --> 00:08:32,340
Do rabbits like carrots?

95
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:41,630
You're in big trouble, Choi Yun.

96
00:08:42,710 --> 00:08:45,330
You have such poor taste in women.

97
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,970
Don't make me sad anymore.

98
00:08:53,330 --> 00:08:57,060
Make me sad again, and I'll really die then.

99
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:19,660
[I'll wait by your house. I'll wait till you get home
- From: Your Yeongwoo]

100
00:09:26,450 --> 00:09:27,720
Sorry.

101
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,690
Pork.

102
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:41,830
Did he tell me to buy the front leg? Or back leg?

103
00:09:41,830 --> 00:09:43,950
Or was it the side?

104
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:48,390
I'm such a blockhead.

105
00:09:48,390 --> 00:09:50,820
I should just die!

106
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:56,330
You know how much I worked
to get that shirt? Give it back...

107
00:09:56,330 --> 00:10:00,950
Brats like this should rot in jail!

108
00:10:00,950 --> 00:10:05,420
She doesn't know any better.
Let it go, why don't you?

109
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:07,840
Why make a big deal over stealing just one shirt?

110
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,770
Just one shirt?

111
00:10:09,770 --> 00:10:13,420
With just this one shirt, I can feed my whole family!

112
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:17,540
It's hard enough as is these days!

113
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:19,530
Why did you steal it?

114
00:10:19,530 --> 00:10:24,380
Didn't Galchi teach you that it's bad to steal clothes?

115
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:27,140
- I gave money.
- You did?

116
00:10:27,910 --> 00:10:33,840
Sure, you paid! You only gave me a dollar
and it costs $28!

117
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:36,080
She wasn't really stealing then.

118
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:39,470
What? Do you like her or something?

119
00:10:39,470 --> 00:10:46,220
All the guys are after her in this area!

120
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:51,290
If you don't put her in jail today, you'll be sorry!

121
00:10:51,290 --> 00:10:53,690
What are you crying for?

122
00:10:53,690 --> 00:10:55,540
Ma'am. Calm down!

123
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:58,840
Huh, what are you crying for?

124
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:02,280
Ma'am! Calm down!

125
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:04,150
Please, sit down, ma'am!

126
00:11:04,150 --> 00:11:06,170
Let's talk about this.

127
00:11:10,620 --> 00:11:14,790
Do not judge. Lead him down the righteous path.

128
00:11:14,790 --> 00:11:21,890
Lead him, I pray, not in the path of ease and comfort,

129
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:24,045
but under the stress and spur
of difficulties and challenge.

130
00:11:24,045 --> 00:11:26,200
Here let him learn to stand up in the storm,

131
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:30,280
here let him learn compassion for those who fail.

132
00:11:31,490 --> 00:11:37,420
Then I, his father, will dare to whisper

133
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:41,170
"I have not lived in vain."

134
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:48,700
That was Audrey, reciting MacArthur's "Build Me a Son."

135
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:55,470
The song playing is "For The One"

136
00:11:55,470 --> 00:11:59,420
by Korea's top singer, Choi Yun.

137
00:11:59,420 --> 00:12:03,850
Choi Yun is Audrey's son.

138
00:12:03,850 --> 00:12:08,750
And we'll finish up with this song.

139
00:12:09,092 --> 00:12:10,714
Great job today.

140
00:12:20,810 --> 00:12:24,340
You should have your own show!

141
00:12:24,340 --> 00:12:28,020
- Oh, you're too kind!
- Right?

142
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:32,230
I should tell my boss to give you a show!

143
00:12:32,230 --> 00:12:34,060
If I ask you to do a show,
you are not allowed to say no.

144
00:12:34,060 --> 00:12:36,780
That's just too much. Stop it.

145
00:12:36,780 --> 00:12:39,350
Thank you so much. The next recording is at 2 p.m.

146
00:12:39,350 --> 00:12:41,810
I'll see you later. Goodbye.

147
00:12:41,810 --> 00:12:44,540
Excuse me. Let's talk for a minute.

148
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:45,560
Yes?

149
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:50,480
A couple days ago, there was a morning
special adoption show, right?

150
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:53,180
- Yes, there was.
- There was a guy on it who...

151
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:55,370
Oh, they must be twins!

152
00:12:55,370 --> 00:12:58,180
How cute.

153
00:12:59,450 --> 00:13:01,960
Sorry, l will contact you later.

154
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:04,860
Oh? Okay. Thank you. Goodbye.

155
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:09,020
I'm sorry, but can I hold your baby?

156
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:12,750
How adorable!

157
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:15,870
May I feed him?

158
00:13:16,430 --> 00:13:19,060
Want some milk?

159
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:23,780
You don't want it? He doesn't want any.

160
00:13:23,780 --> 00:13:27,990
Here you go. Your twins are too cute.

161
00:13:27,990 --> 00:13:31,750
I want to raise twins, too.

162
00:13:34,050 --> 00:13:37,260
Your mother must feel so happy!

163
00:14:25,770 --> 00:14:28,780
It hurts...

164
00:14:30,220 --> 00:14:32,470
Gently!

165
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:21,870
Wake up!

166
00:17:22,870 --> 00:17:26,320
The sun is up, you guys!

167
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:27,700
Hanchae!

168
00:17:30,850 --> 00:17:34,270
Eww! You all disgust me.

169
00:17:34,270 --> 00:17:38,000
If only I could put you back into my stomach!

170
00:17:38,950 --> 00:17:42,770
Sukchae, wake up. Wake up!

171
00:17:43,930 --> 00:17:46,910
Get up!

172
00:17:46,910 --> 00:17:49,140
Eunchae! Wake up!

173
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:55,440
Where's Eunchae?

174
00:17:56,940 --> 00:18:01,110
Would she fit beneath the bed, Mom?

175
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:05,410
She's probably bailing Yun
out of something crazy he did.

176
00:18:05,410 --> 00:18:09,560
He's not causing trouble, he's a genius.
You're so stupid!

177
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:10,840
Why you little...

178
00:18:11,990 --> 00:18:15,660
You'd hit your own mother?

179
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:17,210
That's what I'm saying!

180
00:18:17,210 --> 00:18:21,280
Sorry! Sorry, Mom!

181
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:23,440
That really hurt!

182
00:18:33,610 --> 00:18:38,110
I think that girl with the thick lips recognizes you.

183
00:18:38,110 --> 00:18:40,780
She probably thinks I just look familiar.

184
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:50,970
Eat. Hard boiled eggs in saunas are the best!

185
00:18:50,970 --> 00:18:53,580
You should have gone somewhere else! Why here?

186
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:55,780
If we're caught, we're dead!

187
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:57,820
Just eat it.

188
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:11,800
You found us!

189
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:14,750
So this is what a sauna looks like.

190
00:19:14,750 --> 00:19:15,630
Right?

191
00:19:15,630 --> 00:19:18,300
- It's fun.
- Told you.

192
00:19:19,390 --> 00:19:23,560
Hey, not you, too!

193
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:25,770
What will you do if another scandal breaks loose?

194
00:19:25,770 --> 00:19:28,020
I got it. I'll be careful.

195
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:34,220
I don't have makeup on. They won't recognize me.

196
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:42,920
- Fruit ice cream is killer here.
- Yeah. We should come here all the time.

197
00:19:48,484 --> 00:19:50,130
Yeah, it is him.

198
00:19:59,910 --> 00:20:01,320
Isn't that Choi Yun?

199
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:03,270
- Where?
- Really?

200
00:20:03,270 --> 00:20:05,030
- It is him!
- Choi Yun!

201
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:28,810
What should we do?
What do we do, Eunchae?

202
00:20:28,810 --> 00:20:34,110
I'll cause a distraction. You guys sneak out, okay?

203
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:18,000
Why are you crying?

204
00:21:28,420 --> 00:21:33,430
Why are you crying?

205
00:21:33,430 --> 00:21:36,570
Ma'am! What am I going to do?

206
00:21:36,570 --> 00:21:39,540
What's the matter?

207
00:21:55,630 --> 00:22:00,600
Did someone hit you?

208
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:02,360
No...

209
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:07,730
My butt was burning...

210
00:22:07,730 --> 00:22:09,020
What?

211
00:22:09,020 --> 00:22:12,070
The sauna's really hot, ma'am.

212
00:22:12,070 --> 00:22:13,660
How embarrassing!

213
00:22:22,060 --> 00:22:24,070
How embarrassing.

214
00:22:38,110 --> 00:22:41,550
Yun. Where are you?

215
00:22:41,550 --> 00:22:43,870
Olympic Parkway.

216
00:22:43,870 --> 00:22:45,390
Olympic Parkway?

217
00:22:45,390 --> 00:22:48,240
I'm going to drive Minju home and come home.

218
00:22:48,240 --> 00:22:52,360
Hey, you're bleeding! Does it sting? It stings, huh?

219
00:22:53,510 --> 00:22:55,440
Why weren't you more careful?

220
00:22:55,440 --> 00:22:58,670
Oh, Minju fell and scratched her knee.

221
00:22:58,670 --> 00:23:00,790
You should have been more careful.

222
00:23:01,850 --> 00:23:05,670
It's okay. I can take the bus.

223
00:23:05,670 --> 00:23:06,990
Okay.

224
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:10,580
Mother.

225
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:17,680
You look normal, but how sad.

226
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:19,340
Here.

227
00:23:20,110 --> 00:23:21,270
Thank you.

228
00:23:21,270 --> 00:23:25,290
Let's go, Mother. She at least looks normal.

229
00:23:25,290 --> 00:23:29,200
Her parents must be so disappointed.

230
00:24:12,625 --> 00:24:14,550
Sorry.

231
00:25:20,840 --> 00:25:22,730
Did you eat?

232
00:25:25,810 --> 00:25:27,760
You didn't eat, did you?

233
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:30,350
You don't look like you did.

234
00:25:34,460 --> 00:25:36,890
You like me that much?

235
00:25:39,180 --> 00:25:41,780
What's so great about me that you'd

236
00:25:41,780 --> 00:25:46,000
come all the way here from Australia?

237
00:25:47,890 --> 00:25:50,280
Do you know anyone in Korea?

238
00:25:51,910 --> 00:25:55,690
You don't even know anyone here,
and yet you still came for me?

239
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:02,900
We didn't even get to talk that much.

240
00:26:04,860 --> 00:26:07,770
And I'm not someone men fall for at first sight.

241
00:26:13,170 --> 00:26:16,910
In any case, thank you...

242
00:26:16,910 --> 00:26:19,560
For liking a girl like me.

243
00:26:26,140 --> 00:26:29,350
I don't have much to offer, but do you
want to have dinner at my place?

244
00:26:30,670 --> 00:26:32,170
Let's go.

245
00:26:34,820 --> 00:26:39,080
I can't give you my heart, but I can give you food.

246
00:26:40,350 --> 00:26:41,970
Sorry...

247
00:26:44,080 --> 00:26:46,110
Let's go.

248
00:26:59,280 --> 00:27:02,820
This is Yun's house and our house is over here.

249
00:27:09,850 --> 00:27:12,390
but my house is this way...

250
00:27:13,930 --> 00:27:17,960
Hey, not there!

251
00:27:24,170 --> 00:27:27,830
This isn't our house...

252
00:27:27,830 --> 00:27:29,560
We have to get out!

253
00:27:31,940 --> 00:27:34,170
We'll be in trouble if she comes home!

254
00:27:34,170 --> 00:27:36,460
We have to leave!

255
00:27:41,240 --> 00:27:44,390
We'll get in so much trouble.

256
00:27:44,390 --> 00:27:46,020
Come on...

257
00:27:59,090 --> 00:28:03,610
She probably had her reasons.
No one would ditch their child like that.

258
00:28:03,610 --> 00:28:09,065
Stuff happens.
Maybe she was too poor to even feed me milk

259
00:28:09,065 --> 00:28:11,750
and gave me up so I could have a better life.

260
00:28:22,010 --> 00:28:24,660
Got the same eyes as your mother's.

261
00:28:24,660 --> 00:28:28,400
Truth will prevail in the end.

262
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:30,730
The ancient scholars were very brilliant

263
00:28:30,730 --> 00:28:34,180
to create such words of wisdom.

264
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:44,550
I'll make a lot of money and go back to Korea.

265
00:28:45,540 --> 00:28:47,880
I'll meet my poor mother one day.

266
00:28:47,880 --> 00:28:52,890
I'll buy her some pretty clothes,
some BBQ meat, and a beautiful house.

267
00:28:54,930 --> 00:28:59,890
Mom, I'll go there and let you live in luxury.

268
00:28:59,890 --> 00:29:01,510
Just wait five years!

269
00:30:00,147 --> 00:30:02,513
[Goodbye, my love]

270
00:30:11,670 --> 00:30:14,310
Oh, how sad...

271
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:17,230
Ma'am!

272
00:30:17,230 --> 00:30:19,170
Oh, Eunchae, you're here?

273
00:30:19,860 --> 00:30:21,710
Are you crying?

274
00:30:23,468 --> 00:30:26,570
Stella is so tragic.

275
00:30:26,570 --> 00:30:28,480
Stella?

276
00:30:28,480 --> 00:30:31,620
Stella from "The Last Concert."

277
00:30:31,620 --> 00:30:35,070
You've never watched "The Last Concert"?

278
00:30:35,070 --> 00:30:36,690
No.

279
00:30:36,690 --> 00:30:41,470
Stella is a sad girl who comes out in the movie,

280
00:30:41,470 --> 00:30:44,910
She has leukemia and

281
00:30:44,910 --> 00:30:49,830
later dies as she watches her lover's concert.

282
00:30:49,830 --> 00:30:52,030
Oh...

283
00:30:52,030 --> 00:30:57,780
How can her life be so tragic? Her mother dies...

284
00:30:57,780 --> 00:31:01,320
Her father has an affair and flees with his lover...

285
00:31:01,320 --> 00:31:04,680
And then to abandon Richard, who she loved.

286
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:07,210
How hard it must have been to die and leave him...

287
00:31:08,710 --> 00:31:12,250
Take it easy, ma'am. It's just a movie.

288
00:31:12,250 --> 00:31:15,550
It's just a movie, but my heart aches so badly!

289
00:31:16,980 --> 00:31:21,080
I've watched it five times,
and every time my heart hurts.

290
00:31:22,990 --> 00:31:25,940
Son, my son!

291
00:31:28,310 --> 00:31:34,200
Don't you want to cheer me up? Go shopping with me.

292
00:31:36,260 --> 00:31:40,310
It's not Yun...

293
00:31:45,160 --> 00:31:47,120
Who is that man?

294
00:31:48,350 --> 00:31:54,190
He's... Someone I sort of know.

295
00:31:54,190 --> 00:31:58,650
He came into the wrong house. I'm sorry, ma'am.

296
00:32:21,280 --> 00:32:23,590
What's with him?

297
00:32:23,590 --> 00:32:24,430
Hey!

298
00:32:24,430 --> 00:32:26,670
Why is that man crying?

299
00:32:26,670 --> 00:32:30,830
I did something wrong. He must be hurt because of me.

300
00:32:33,740 --> 00:32:37,230
But why did he look at me that way?

301
00:32:37,230 --> 00:32:38,750
Mister.

302
00:32:40,340 --> 00:32:41,910
Mister!

303
00:32:43,190 --> 00:32:44,970
Mister!

304
00:32:44,970 --> 00:32:46,610
Mister!

305
00:32:49,630 --> 00:32:52,150
Mister!

306
00:33:03,340 --> 00:33:06,010
I'm sorry!

307
00:33:06,010 --> 00:33:12,570
I'm flattered, but I already have someone I like...

308
00:33:12,570 --> 00:33:15,430
There's no room for you...

309
00:33:19,550 --> 00:33:21,440
I'm sorry!

310
00:33:55,490 --> 00:33:57,260
Eat rice!

311
00:33:59,310 --> 00:34:01,270
Hey, Galchi, eat.

312
00:34:01,270 --> 00:34:05,690
I told you! I'm not going to talk to you anymore!

313
00:34:07,320 --> 00:34:10,330
I'm sorry... I said sorry.

314
00:34:11,080 --> 00:34:15,110
Talk to me, please?

315
00:34:15,110 --> 00:34:17,070
Running around and stealing stuff...

316
00:34:17,070 --> 00:34:19,830
I'm embarrassed to death because of you.

317
00:34:19,830 --> 00:34:22,700
What a pain!

318
00:34:23,530 --> 00:34:26,790
I won't do it again.

319
00:34:26,790 --> 00:34:29,160
I won't.

320
00:34:29,160 --> 00:34:32,780
You always say that!

321
00:34:32,780 --> 00:34:34,620
Are you stupid, mom?

322
00:34:42,030 --> 00:34:44,980
Didn't you know your mom was stupid?

323
00:34:44,980 --> 00:34:47,630
If she doesn't know, you can just keep telling her.

324
00:34:47,630 --> 00:34:49,930
You can teach her, you brat!

325
00:34:54,630 --> 00:34:58,080
You think you know everything.

326
00:34:58,080 --> 00:35:00,320
You better eat, now!

327
00:35:03,350 --> 00:35:05,620
You know I'm a gangster, right?

328
00:35:05,620 --> 00:35:08,350
Do you want to get hit or do you want to eat?

329
00:35:17,110 --> 00:35:18,670
I said eat!

330
00:35:28,080 --> 00:35:29,670
Drink water...

331
00:35:32,010 --> 00:35:33,850
Drink it!

332
00:35:37,170 --> 00:35:41,820
Even though your mom lives her life like that,

333
00:35:41,820 --> 00:35:47,340
even though she's an idiot, she didn't leave you.

334
00:36:31,197 --> 00:36:32,278
Hello?

335
00:36:34,338 --> 00:36:35,980
Hello?

336
00:36:40,235 --> 00:36:44,160
It's me. Danny.

337
00:36:44,160 --> 00:36:45,560
Muhyeok.

338
00:36:45,560 --> 00:36:47,820
How are you?

339
00:36:47,820 --> 00:36:51,180
Is Korea good?

340
00:36:51,577 --> 00:36:58,221
Yeah, thanks to you. I checked into
a really nice hotel with the money you gave me.

341
00:36:59,393 --> 00:37:08,290
You were right. It's a lot of money.
Enough to last me a lifetime. Thank you.

342
00:37:08,290 --> 00:37:12,910
Why aren't you speaking in Korean?
Is there something wrong?

343
00:37:13,822 --> 00:37:18,158
I called because I wanted to ask you something.

344
00:37:21,111 --> 00:37:25,455
How long did the doctors say I have to live?

345
00:37:26,826 --> 00:37:34,493
I heard I was dying, but I didn't find out
how much time I have left.

346
00:37:35,630 --> 00:37:36,830
Muhyeok.

347
00:37:38,899 --> 00:37:41,468
Do I have at least...

348
00:37:45,227 --> 00:37:47,482
A year?

349
00:37:52,018 --> 00:37:53,944
Not even...

350
00:37:57,740 --> 00:38:00,193
A year?

351
00:38:29,700 --> 00:38:32,830
Son, my son!

352
00:38:34,060 --> 00:38:36,860
Don't you want to cheer me up?

353
00:38:36,860 --> 00:38:38,370
Who is that man?

354
00:39:20,675 --> 00:39:22,243
[Choi Yun's Midnight Concert]

355
00:41:18,770 --> 00:41:21,210
Let's take ten!

356
00:41:37,180 --> 00:41:39,060
It's your first time seeing me dance, huh?

357
00:41:39,060 --> 00:41:42,070
How was it? The director says it's corny.

358
00:41:42,070 --> 00:41:43,160
It was.

359
00:41:44,450 --> 00:41:48,150
Really? You think it's corny, too?

360
00:41:48,150 --> 00:41:49,270
Yes.

361
00:41:51,160 --> 00:41:53,480
- It's corny?
- Huh?

362
00:41:53,480 --> 00:41:55,640
I'm not doing the show. I'm going home.

363
00:41:55,640 --> 00:41:58,340
Hey, what's wrong?

364
00:41:58,340 --> 00:42:00,380
Is it really corny?

365
00:42:00,380 --> 00:42:02,170
- Did I say that?
- Yes.

366
00:42:02,170 --> 00:42:04,180
- When?
- Right now!

367
00:42:04,180 --> 00:42:07,800
No. It was amazing.

368
00:42:07,800 --> 00:42:09,350
So killer!

369
00:42:10,280 --> 00:42:12,740
You definitely said it was corny.

370
00:42:12,740 --> 00:42:16,380
I didn't!

371
00:42:19,210 --> 00:42:20,820
Is it really killer!

372
00:42:20,820 --> 00:42:22,500
Yes.

373
00:42:24,410 --> 00:42:27,440
When other people say something,
you act as if nothing happened

374
00:42:27,440 --> 00:42:31,490
but when I say something...
You act like it's the end of the world.

375
00:42:31,490 --> 00:42:33,620
Of course! You always give me a hard time.

376
00:42:33,620 --> 00:42:35,750
Am I your pet? Your toy?

377
00:42:35,950 --> 00:42:38,100
No. A goddess.

378
00:42:38,990 --> 00:42:43,500
You're my goddess. Did you not know that?

379
00:42:43,500 --> 00:42:47,410
If you like it, it's good no matter what.

380
00:42:47,410 --> 00:42:51,230
If you don't like it, it's the end of my world.

381
00:42:54,400 --> 00:42:56,530
It was killer, right?

382
00:42:58,070 --> 00:42:59,300
Yeah.

383
00:43:12,180 --> 00:43:13,800
What are you doing here?

384
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:15,890
I have a shoot close to here.

385
00:43:15,890 --> 00:43:20,040
I heard Yun singing. I'm taking a small break.

386
00:43:20,930 --> 00:43:23,020
I missed him.

387
00:43:23,770 --> 00:43:26,540
You should have called.

388
00:43:26,540 --> 00:43:28,020
Where are you shooting?

389
00:43:28,020 --> 00:43:31,100
Nearby. When are you singing?

390
00:43:31,100 --> 00:43:33,240
In a little while.

391
00:43:54,660 --> 00:44:01,180
When I think of my mother,
I'm grateful and I start to cry.

392
00:44:02,070 --> 00:44:07,940
For giving birth to me and raising me so well.

393
00:44:08,600 --> 00:44:11,820
Moving me with her endless love.

394
00:44:13,180 --> 00:44:16,950
Mom, you are my sunshine. My world.

395
00:44:19,120 --> 00:44:21,550
I love you, mom. I love you.

396
00:44:44,670 --> 00:44:46,780
Why are you here?

397
00:44:46,780 --> 00:44:48,300
To see Yun.

398
00:44:49,240 --> 00:44:50,680
Let's go.

399
00:44:50,680 --> 00:44:53,760
But there's still time until the shooting.

400
00:44:54,360 --> 00:44:56,010
Let go.

401
00:44:56,660 --> 00:45:00,570
Why are you doing this? Stop it!

402
00:45:31,170 --> 00:45:33,100
Stop right there, Jo Yeongwoo!

403
00:45:38,650 --> 00:45:40,460
Let go of her hand.

404
00:45:40,460 --> 00:45:42,720
Go back and do your little dance.

405
00:45:42,720 --> 00:45:44,500
You better let go!

406
00:45:48,130 --> 00:45:51,790
Minju's my girl. Let go of her hand.

407
00:45:56,490 --> 00:45:57,980
You starting a fight?

408
00:45:57,980 --> 00:46:00,500
I told you to let go.

409
00:46:01,720 --> 00:46:04,610
Fine. Let's end it today.

410
00:46:06,580 --> 00:46:10,300
Say it now. Me or Choi Yun?

411
00:46:13,770 --> 00:46:15,840
Me or Choi Yun?

412
00:46:23,230 --> 00:46:26,060
Can you both let go of my wrists?

413
00:46:32,860 --> 00:46:36,380
We're going to be on the front page
of the news tomorrow.

414
00:46:37,580 --> 00:46:39,810
My dad is going to explode again.

415
00:46:39,810 --> 00:46:42,770
Didn't you break up with him?

416
00:46:42,770 --> 00:46:44,170
I did.

417
00:46:44,170 --> 00:46:45,410
Kang Minju!

418
00:46:45,410 --> 00:46:49,350
I did, but I don't think he can.

419
00:46:50,450 --> 00:46:54,390
Do you want to see me die today?

420
00:46:54,390 --> 00:46:56,930
Are you two competing?

421
00:46:56,930 --> 00:46:59,450
Always saying you're going to die.

422
00:46:59,450 --> 00:47:01,670
It's getting so old.

423
00:47:02,420 --> 00:47:05,190
You guys will die over a woman?

424
00:47:06,360 --> 00:47:08,720
You guys will die over love?

425
00:47:10,968 --> 00:47:12,480
This is exhausting.

426
00:47:14,080 --> 00:47:17,000
I should stop playing with kids.

427
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:18,510
- Minju!
- Minju.

428
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:26,340
I'm sorry, but I don't believe in love.

429
00:47:28,010 --> 00:47:33,520
And guys like you who always talk about love

430
00:47:33,520 --> 00:47:35,210
I especially don't believe.

431
00:47:40,670 --> 00:47:42,180
Minju!

432
00:47:46,040 --> 00:47:50,420
Yeongwoo, you said that if I died,
you'd die along with me.

433
00:47:52,520 --> 00:47:57,440
Choi Yun, didn't you say you
loved me more than yourself?

434
00:48:00,620 --> 00:48:02,330
Is that really true?

435
00:48:05,010 --> 00:48:07,090
Could it be the truth?

436
00:48:09,520 --> 00:48:14,270
Could a love like that really exist?

437
00:48:21,010 --> 00:48:22,360
Minju!

438
00:48:24,540 --> 00:48:26,070
Yun!

439
00:48:27,060 --> 00:48:31,100
Save him!

440
00:48:31,100 --> 00:48:33,400
Minju and Yun can't swim!

441
00:48:33,400 --> 00:48:35,980
Neither can swim!

442
00:49:45,750 --> 00:49:48,720
How is Minju?

443
00:49:50,020 --> 00:49:54,650
Don't worry. She's fine.

444
00:50:05,450 --> 00:50:07,770
Yun. Yun!

445
00:51:13,270 --> 00:51:15,530
Stay still!

446
00:51:21,150 --> 00:51:23,190
Would you like to wait a bit?

447
00:51:23,190 --> 00:51:26,490
I'll bring Yun's clothes. Want to wear those?

448
00:51:32,730 --> 00:51:34,060
Mister!

449
00:51:34,890 --> 00:51:36,560
Wait!

450
00:51:38,120 --> 00:51:43,350
You'll catch a cold like that. You'll freeze to death!

451
00:51:43,350 --> 00:51:45,800
You really don't listen, do you?

452
00:51:58,130 --> 00:52:01,640
Mister! Wake up!

453
00:52:02,580 --> 00:52:06,240
Mister! Mister, wake up!

454
00:54:36,700 --> 00:54:41,260
What'd you do all these years?
Not knowing how to swim.

455
00:54:41,260 --> 00:54:43,630
It seems like you like that girl.

456
00:54:43,630 --> 00:54:45,530
You must have been embarrassed a bit.

457
00:54:55,400 --> 00:54:57,900
Are you the person who saved us?

458
00:54:57,900 --> 00:54:59,130
Maybe...

459
00:54:59,640 --> 00:55:00,850
Thanks, bro.

460
00:55:04,310 --> 00:55:06,960
You don't have a brother, right?

461
00:55:07,810 --> 00:55:08,900
Nope.

462
00:55:09,770 --> 00:55:12,840
Want me to be your brother?

463
00:55:15,370 --> 00:55:19,080
Want to be my little brother?

464
00:55:19,080 --> 00:55:20,360
We'll see.

465
00:55:21,190 --> 00:55:22,500
Don't want to?

466
00:55:23,940 --> 00:55:25,400
Then don't!

467
00:55:42,480 --> 00:55:44,250
Sure.

468
00:55:46,170 --> 00:55:47,690
I'll be your little bro.

469
00:56:16,841 --> 00:56:18,376
[Episode 4 Preview]

470
00:56:18,376 --> 00:56:20,771
He seems totally into me.

471
00:56:20,771 --> 00:56:22,527
Eunchae said she slept with a guy.

472
00:56:22,527 --> 00:56:25,121
No, it's not what you think!

473
00:56:26,671 --> 00:56:27,901
Now I'm seeing things.

474
00:56:29,791 --> 00:56:33,663
[Sorry, I want to be by your side]

475
00:56:43,431 --> 00:56:47,831
Don't be shy.
This is what you do when you're dating.

476
00:56:47,831 --> 00:56:50,307
Are you being shy again?

477
00:56:53,611 --> 00:56:54,712
[I wanted to call out Love's name just once]

478
00:56:54,712 --> 00:56:57,169
Son!

479
00:56:57,169 --> 00:56:59,088
Yun is sleeping.

480
00:56:59,488 --> 00:57:01,208
Where's the medicine?
